WEBVTT

00:00.660 --> 00:04.580
Let's say that I've
got 2 Chuck Norrises,

00:04.580 --> 00:06.640
or maybe it's Chuck Norri.

00:06.640 --> 00:13.090
And to that I am going to
add another 3 Chuck Norrises.

00:13.090 --> 00:15.130
So I'm going to add
another 3 Chuck Norrises.

00:15.130 --> 00:16.990
And this might seem
a little bit obvious,

00:16.990 --> 00:20.160
but how many Chuck
Norrises do I now have?

00:20.160 --> 00:22.940
Well, 2 Chuck Norrises,
we can represent this

00:22.940 --> 00:26.610
as literally a Chuck
Norris plus a Chuck Norris.

00:26.610 --> 00:28.280
So let me do that,
a Chuck Norris

00:28.280 --> 00:31.600
plus another Chuck
Norris, 2 Chuck Norrises.

00:31.600 --> 00:33.610
You could also do this
2 times Chuck Norris,

00:33.610 --> 00:35.770
and this is just another
way of representing it.

00:35.770 --> 00:40.900
And 3 Chuck Norrises-- you
could do that as a Chuck Norris

00:40.900 --> 00:45.290
plus a Chuck Norris plus
another Chuck Norris.

00:45.290 --> 00:47.300
And so we would
have a grand total--

00:47.300 --> 00:50.000
and this might be
very simple for you.

00:50.000 --> 00:52.660
But you would have a
grand total of 1, 2, 3, 4,

00:52.660 --> 00:54.450
5 Chuck Norrises.

00:54.450 --> 01:00.582
So this would be equal
to 5 Chuck Norrises.

01:00.582 --> 01:02.540
Now, let's get a little
bit more abstract here.

01:02.540 --> 01:05.209
Chuck Norris is a
very tangible thing.

01:05.209 --> 01:07.330
So let's go to a
little bit more of

01:07.330 --> 01:09.380
traditional algebraic notation.

01:09.380 --> 01:13.720
If I have 2x's and
remember, you could

01:13.720 --> 01:16.260
do this as 2x's or 2 times x.

01:19.370 --> 01:23.220
And to that, I would add
3x's How many x's do I have?

01:23.220 --> 01:25.450
Well, once again,
2x's, that's 2 times x.

01:25.450 --> 01:27.410
You could do that
as an x plus an x.

01:27.410 --> 01:29.270
We don't know what
the value of x is.

01:29.270 --> 01:32.460
But whatever that value is,
we can add it to itself.

01:32.460 --> 01:34.780
And then 3x's are they're
going to be that value.

01:34.780 --> 01:37.590
Let me do that in
that same green color.

01:37.590 --> 01:41.640
3x's are going to be that
value plus that value plus

01:41.640 --> 01:43.460
whatever that value is.

01:43.460 --> 01:46.300
And so how many
x's do I now have?

01:46.300 --> 01:50.810
Well, I'm going to
have 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 x's.

01:50.810 --> 01:57.119
So 2x plus 3x is equal to 5x.

01:57.119 --> 01:59.660
And if you think about it, all
we really did-- and hopefully,

01:59.660 --> 02:01.160
you conceptually
get it-- is we just

02:01.160 --> 02:03.950
added the 2 numbers that
were multiplying the x.

02:03.950 --> 02:07.350
And these numbers, the 2 or the
3, they're called coefficients.

02:07.350 --> 02:09.860
Very fancy word, but it's
just this constant number,

02:09.860 --> 02:12.980
this regular number that's
multiplied by the variable.

02:12.980 --> 02:16.814
You just added the 2 and
the 3, to get your 5x.

02:16.814 --> 02:18.730
Now, let's think about
this a little bit more.

02:18.730 --> 02:21.400
Let's go back to this original
expression, the 2 Chuck

02:21.400 --> 02:23.400
Norrises plus 3 Chuck Norrises.

02:23.400 --> 02:27.380
Let's say, to that,
we were to add

02:27.380 --> 02:31.680
to some type of a-- let's we
were to add 7 plums over here.

02:31.680 --> 02:34.050
So this is my drawing of a plum.

02:34.050 --> 02:38.410
So we have 7 plums plus 2 Chuck
Norrises plus 3 Chuck Norrises.

02:38.410 --> 02:41.040
And let's say that I
add another 2 plums.

02:41.040 --> 02:42.950
I add another 2 plums here.

02:42.950 --> 02:44.990
So what this whole thing be?

02:44.990 --> 02:48.170
Well, I wouldn't add the 7
to the 2 to the 3 plus the 2.

02:48.170 --> 02:49.750
We're adding
different things here.

02:49.750 --> 02:51.950
You have 2 Chuck Norrises
and 3 Chuck Norrises,

02:51.950 --> 02:54.895
so they're still going to
simplify to 5 Chuck Norrises. .

02:54.895 --> 02:57.020
And then we would separately
think about the plums.

02:57.020 --> 02:59.700
We have 7 plums, and we're
adding another 2 plums.

02:59.700 --> 03:01.820
We're going to have 9 plums.

03:01.820 --> 03:06.920
Plus 9 plums, so this simplifies
to five Chuck Norrises and 9

03:06.920 --> 03:07.810
plums.

03:07.810 --> 03:12.360
Similarly, over here,
instead of just 2x plus 3x,

03:12.360 --> 03:21.970
if I had 7y plus 2x plus 3x
plus 2y, what do I now have?

03:21.970 --> 03:24.050
Well, I can't add the
x's and the y's.

03:24.050 --> 03:26.420
They could very well
represent a different number.

03:26.420 --> 03:28.590
So all I can do is
really add the x's.

03:28.590 --> 03:30.022
And then I get the 5x.

03:30.022 --> 03:31.480
And then, I'd
separately add the y.

03:31.480 --> 03:35.800
If I have 7y's and to that I add
2y's, I'm going to have 9y's.

03:35.800 --> 03:38.170
If I have 7 of something
and I add 2 of something,

03:38.170 --> 03:40.440
I now have 9 of that something.

03:40.440 --> 03:42.710
So I'm going to have 9y's.

03:42.710 --> 03:44.235
So you add that.

03:44.235 --> 03:45.740
Do that in a different color.

03:45.740 --> 03:48.700
You add this and this.

03:48.700 --> 03:50.140
You get that.

03:50.140 --> 03:54.070
You add the x's.

03:54.070 --> 03:56.064
You get that right over there.

03:56.064 --> 03:57.730
So hopefully, that
makes a little sense.

03:57.730 --> 03:59.313
Actually I'll throw
out one more idea.

03:59.313 --> 04:04.530
So given this, what would happen
if I were to have 2x plus 1

04:04.530 --> 04:08.407
plus 7x plus 5?

04:08.407 --> 04:09.990
Well, once again,
you might be tempted

04:09.990 --> 04:11.350
to add the 2 plus
the 1, but they're

04:11.350 --> 04:12.220
adding different things.

04:12.220 --> 04:12.970
These are 2x's.

04:12.970 --> 04:14.910
This is just the number 1.

04:14.910 --> 04:17.490
So you really just have
to add the x's together.

04:17.490 --> 04:19.430
So you're going to
say, well, I got 2x's.

04:19.430 --> 04:21.550
And I'm going to
add 7x's to that.

04:21.550 --> 04:23.507
Well, that means
I now have 9x's.

04:23.507 --> 04:25.090
And then, separately,
you'd say, well,

04:25.090 --> 04:27.130
I've got just the
abstract number 1.

04:27.130 --> 04:28.460
And then I've got another 5.

04:28.460 --> 04:32.280
1 plus 5 is going
to be equal to 6.
